Here's how to handle each scenario with modern MSTest (3.9+/3.10+):

## 1. Windows-only tests — `[OSCondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    var value = Registry.GetValue(@"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\MyApp", "Setting", null);
    Assert.IsNotNull(value);
}
```

The test is **skipped** (not failed) on Linux/macOS.

## 2. Skip in CI — `[CICondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
public void GpuRendering_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    var result = GpuRenderer.Render(scene);
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

This excludes the test when common CI environment variables are detected (e.g., `CI`, `TF_BUILD`, `GITHUB_ACTIONS`).

## 3. Flaky external API — `[Retry]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)]
public async Task WeatherApi_ReturnsForecast()
{
    var forecast = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync("Seattle");
    Assert.IsNotNull(forecast);
    Assert.IsNotEmpty(forecast.Days);
}
```

The test retries up to 3 times before reporting failure. Use **only** for genuinely flaky external dependencies — not to mask race conditions.

## 4. Cleanup even on failure — `[TestCleanup]`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public sealed class TempFileTests
{
    private string _tempFilePath = string.Empty;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFilePath = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        FileProcessor.Process(_tempFilePath);
        var content = File.ReadAllText(_tempFilePath);
        Assert.Contains("expected", content);
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs even if the test throws
        if (File.Exists(_tempFilePath))
        {
            File.Delete(_tempFilePath);
        }
    }
}
```

`[TestCleanup]` is guaranteed to run after each test method regardless of pass/fail. For `IDisposable` resources, you can also implement `IDisposable`/`IAsyncDisposable` on the test class — MSTest calls `Dispose` after cleanup.

---

**Summary of attributes:**

| Scenario | Attribute | MSTest version |
|----------|-----------|----------------|
| OS-specific | `[OSCondition(...)]` | 3.10+ |
| Skip in CI | `[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]` | 3.10+ |
| Retry flaky | `[Retry(N)]` | 3.9+ |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` | All versions |
